{{also|intolérant}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|intolérant}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-us-intolerant.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Unable or [[indisposed]] to [[tolerate]], [[endure]] or [[bear]].
#: ''I am lactose-'''intolerant''', so I can't drink milk.''
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2013|author=Sarah Taylor|title=Vegetarian to Vegan: Give Up Dairy, Give Up Eggs for Good|passage=When our bodies no longer create the enzyme needed to break down lactose, we can become '''intolerant''' to it.}}
#* '''1892''', Harry Marshall Ward, ''The Oak: A Popular Introduction to Forest-botany''
#*:The oak, as is well known, is a slow-growing, dicotyledonous tree of peculiar spreading habit, and very '''intolerant''' of shade.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1751|author=John Arbuthnot|title=An Essay Concerning the Effects of Air on Human Bodies|passage=The powers of human bodies being limited and '''intolerant''' of excesses.}}
# Not [[tolerant]]; [[close-minded]] about new or different [[idea]]s; indisposed to tolerate contrary [[opinion]]s or [[belief]]s; impatient of [[dissent]] or [[opposition]]; denying or refusing the right of private opinion or choice in others; inclined to [[persecute]] or [[suppress]] dissent.

